  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "分子基因學",
    "sub_ename": "MOLECULAR GENETICS",
    "describe_ch": "本課程提供有關控制細胞生物活動的分子基因學原理和重要信息，特別著重在細菌。這包括細胞過程與基因調控機制的協調、重組 DNA 技術基本概念的概述、應用分子遺傳學技術的基本概念以及生命科學實驗室中最常用的核心方法。這些主題結合生化和基因信息，使學生能夠更深入地了解與現代生物學其他領域相關的分子基因學。",
    "describe_eh": "This course provides important information on principles of molecular genetics governing biological activities of living cells with the emphasis on bacteria. This includes the coordination of cellular processes with regulation mechanisms of genes, an overview of fundamental concepts in recombinant DNA technology, the essential concepts of applied molecular genetics techniques, and the core methodologies most applied in life science laboratories. The topics are integrated with biochemical and genomic information, which enables students to gain a deeper understanding of molecular genetics related to other fields of modern biology.",
